From ea1a5ee635e4ecfd8e83855011ddc80d0771c4d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 15:50:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Render HRPT permit data through the same week/month grid as
 every field
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous commit displayed real HRPT data, but through a separately-
styled "Permit Info" card (its own box, status chip, bulleted list) that
looked inconsistent with the rest of the site's native field-schedule
grid (renderSchdWeek/renderSchdMonth).

Instead of a bespoke card, adapt each D1 permit_cache row into the same
shape a Socrata permit object already has (start_date_time/end_date_time/
event_name), so the existing permitDate/permitStartHour/permitTypeBadge
helpers work unmodified, and feed that into the actual grid renderer.
renderSchdWeek/renderSchdMonth now take an optional prefixHtml so the
existing "managed by X, book at Y" disclaimer can still sit above the
grid. Data is fetched once per field and cached on the field object,
same lifetime as a normal field's already-loaded permits.

Removes the now-superseded loadPermitInfoCard and its single-purpose
helpers (_fmtSyncDate, _isStale, _fmtPermitTime) — dead code after this
change, not kept around.
---
 public/TrueSpordo.html | 155 +++++++++++++++--------------------------
 1 file changed, 55 insertions(+), 100 deletions(-)

diff --git a/public/TrueSpordo.html b/public/TrueSpordo.html
index 8e60f80..596ebd3 100644
